## What just shipped

✅ **Phase 4.5 self-serve Persona Builder UI (#21–#28), SHIPPED + LIVE IN PROD 2026-06-15 (PRs #253 backend / #254 frontend / #256 redesign, session `phase-4.5-persona-builder-ui`, CLOSED).**
The whole self-serve builder is now live: a customer connects a feature store → maps columns to the 7 canonical feature groups (LLM-suggested, temp=0, confidence-chipped) → fires a persona-pack build via `sidira_personas` behind the pipeline seam → watches honest-text progress → **evaluates the unpromoted pack** → promotes it as `latest`. Backend (#21–#25, PR #253, squash `1926232`): KMS/local envelope-encrypted feature-store creds (AAD-bound to `customer_id:connection_id`, scoped so legacy crawl-cred blobs still decrypt), Snowflake adapter (connect/test/100-row preview, table_fqn injection-hardened), `column_mapper` service, persona-builds endpoint (POST/GET/JSONL events, BackgroundTask, R2 `v_N` bump + stability gate), persona-packs list/get/promote. Migrations 011+012; redeployed to api.sidira.ai (alembic 012, `feature_store_connections` + `persona_build_runs` tables live, cred mode=local so no KMS key). Frontend (#26–#28, PR #254, squash `da04b0b`): 7-step wizard in crawl-setup instrument posture. **Then redesigned (PR #256, squash `a1a69be`):** the original flow promoted on a single stability scalar and only linked the rich persona view *after* committing — wrong gate. New 5-step flow `Connect · Map · Build · Evaluate · Promote` adds an **Evaluate** step that reads the unpromoted pack from R2 by version (`getPersonaPackDetail` resolves an explicit version regardless of the `latest` pointer) and shows a compact, honest per-persona read (share chips + distinctiveness line that *says so* when a persona isn't distinctive; holdout/Jaccard #7 named as not-yet-shown, never faked). Codex caught + fixed: Promote was reachable before the pack rendered (now gated on a loaded pack whose version matches the build) and a stale-read race after rerun (latest-wins `evalReqRef`). Frontend-only → Amplify auto-build, no redeploy. ⚠️ **DB scope decision: Snowflake-only stays for MVP** (matches ROADMAP:166 + adapter Protocol docstring); generalization to any DB connector is filed as **#255** (kind-dispatch factory + per-vendor schema + UI-by-kind — the `FeatureStore` read-Protocol seam already exists, so it's cheap later).

✅ **Persona-pack v1.1 richness surfaced on the detail page, SHIPPED + LIVE IN PROD 2026-06-15 (PRs #249/#250, session `persona-pack-ui`, CLOSED).**
The producer→consumer v1.1 chain was proven into agent prompts (#247/#248) but the frontend was still v1.0-shaped — centroids, alternative weight schemes, and honesty/stability fields were stored and read by agents yet shown on no page. #249 (squash `56efb34`) adds a server-rendered view: `GET /persona-packs/{id}/detail` → `services/persona_pack_view.py` (`PersonaPackDetail`), which renders the centroid "how this segment compares" block and (on a v1.1 pack) the per-member individual-row block **through `behavioral_profile.py`**, so the salience/grounding/honesty rules that govern what an agent reads also govern what the PM sees — no second implementation to drift. Every weight scheme is shown with an honest reason when one is unavailable; v1.0 packs degrade to an honest empty individual-row state. `has_individual_rows` is derived from row INPUTS, not rendered deltas (codex P2). `/personas/[id]` rebuilt in DESIGN.md §7.6 record voice (paper, mono designators, no glass/motion). #250 (squash `b0967a8`) fixed a subject-verb agreement bug caught on the live page ("1 further trait *sits*…"). Backend redeployed to api.sidira.ai (`56efb34`, no migration); Amplify rebuilt and the fix verified live. Spun out as future work: build-history/draft-pack/promote UI + the stubbed `/personas/new` wizard (blocked on the realigned Phase-4.5 backend #23/#24). **Phase-4.5 ticket realignment** posted in the same session: #24's "import the producer as a library" premise is dead (the `translate_producer_pack` JSON seam exists precisely because the simulator venv can't import `sidira_personas`); #23 retargeted to adapted-feature space; #22 reframed as connector #1 of N (data connectors are pluggable, never Snowflake-only).

✅ **PHASE 5 AUTH + MULTI-TENANCY, FULLY LIVE IN PROD 2026-06-10 (umbrella session `phase-5-auth`, CLOSED).**
Production now runs Clerk sign-in end-to-end: Amplify frontend (Deployment 74) serves Clerk auth pages (#32, PR #153) instead of the temporary Basic-Auth gate; the Caddy proxy forwards the Clerk token via the `X-Sidira-Clerk-Authorization` hop (#149, PRs #158/#159); the backend session gate + per-request multi-tenancy (#29, PR #150) are active (`SIDIRA_CLERK_SECRET_KEY` live on EC2). Tenancy model: **customer = Clerk Organization** — the `organization.created` webhook provisions the `customers` row (#31, PR #152, live + E2E-confirmed). #30 scoping audit found NO live leaks and left a route-walking regression guard + cross-customer isolation matrix in CI (PR #157). Auth-provider portability contract documented in `docs/auth-provider-portability.md` (PR #160). Prod posture: **invite-only beta** — invite users via ORGANIZATION invitations, not instance-level. Verified end-to-end signed-in/signed-out; issue #149 closed with the verification record.

✅ **One-click sample workspace seeding, SHIPPED + LIVE IN PROD 2026-06-09 (PR #161, squash `0c21916`, session `sample-workspace`, CLOSED).**
New orgs land in an empty workspace post-cutover; `POST /sample-workspace` clones the Streamly fixture (6 personas, 2 capabilities) into the caller's own tenant prefix, strictly button-triggered from the wizard/personas empty states. Source hardcoded server-side (tenant isolation), 409 no-clobber, pointers-last + marker-based retry recovery over the CAS-less ArtifactStore protocol. 13 tests; codex 2 rounds, all findings fixed. Deployed both sides (Amplify + EC2) and verified on a real empty org. ⚠️ R2 `customers/streamly_sample/` is the live clone source — never delete. Same day: pre-cutover sims under the legacy `streamly_sample` tenant and the webhook-test customer row were deleted from prod Neon (via codex/psql).

